{
  "$defs": {
    "ProvenancedValue": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A single numeric quantity tagged with its provenance.\n\nConstruct via the classmethods (:meth:`from_document`, :meth:`from_connector`,\n:meth:`assume`, :meth:`derived`) so the ``source`` tag is never forgotten.\n\nA **measured or derived estimate** may also carry a quantitative uncertainty range\n(#760): optional absolute ``low``/``high`` bounds around the central ``value``,\n*orthogonal* to the qualitative ``confidence`` enum. The convention: a document- or\nconnector-verbatim figure is a single value (no band); an estimate whose honest\nrepresentation is \"226 ± ~35 ac\" carries ``low``/``high`` so downstream consumers\n(the bundle, the frontend, the Monte-Carlo engine #271) see the spread as data, not\nprose buried in the citation. The estimate constructors (:meth:`derived`,\n:meth:`assume`, :meth:`from_reference`) take the range inline; :meth:`with_range`\nattaches one to any value (e.g. a document-anchored central with a derived band).",
      "properties": {
        "value": {
          "title": "Value",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "unit": {
          "title": "Unit",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "source": {
          "enum": [
            "document",
            "connector",
            "reference",
            "assumption",
            "derived"
          ],
          "title": "Source",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "citation": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Citation"
        },
        "confidence": {
          "default": "medium",
          "enum": [
            "high",
            "medium",
            "low"
          ],
          "title": "Confidence",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "asof": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Asof"
        },
        "low": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Low"
        },
        "high": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "number"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "High"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "value",
        "unit",
        "source"
      ],
      "title": "ProvenancedValue",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ScenarioAxis": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "One cited driver of the economic argument, published as a band with its sources.\n\nThe typed home of the figures `docs/ECONOMICS.md` §4 carried as prose: the\nauthorized-region (GovCloud) premium, the DCTE tax-base forecasting risk, the jobs-per-MW\nstaffing range, the subsidy-per-job benchmark. ``band`` is ``None`` for a\n**corroboration** axis that asserts no range of its own (the sales-tax-exemption-dominance\nfinding is a qualitative corroboration from other jurisdictions, not a Lima magnitude) —\nthose still carry their sources, so the claim can be checked.\n\n``site_status`` is the prior's ``lima_status``, generalized: whether the band's application\nto *this* site is ``open`` (unresolved), ``comparative`` (a benchmark the site is read\nagainst), or ``context`` (national backdrop). It is what keeps an industry range from\nbeing read as a facility fact.",
      "properties": {
        "key": {
          "title": "Key",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "label": {
          "title": "Label",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "question": {
          "title": "Question",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "band": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/$defs/ScenarioBand"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null
        },
        "tag": {
          "default": "reference",
          "enum": [
            "verified",
            "inference",
            "reference",
            "open"
          ],
          "title": "Tag",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "confidence": {
          "default": "low",
          "enum": [
            "high",
            "medium",
            "low"
          ],
          "title": "Confidence",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "site_status": {
          "default": "open",
          "title": "Site Status",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "drives": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "type": "string"
          },
          "title": "Drives",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "basis": {
          "default": "",
          "title": "Basis",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "sources": {
          "default": [],
          "items": {
            "$ref": "#/$defs/ScenarioSource"
          },
          "title": "Sources",
          "type": "array"
        },
        "resolving_record": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "type": "string"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "default": null,
          "title": "Resolving Record"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "key",
        "label",
        "question"
      ],
      "title": "ScenarioAxis",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ScenarioBand": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "A low/central/high band — the deliverable, never a point estimate.\n\n``high > low`` is enforced: a \"band\" that collapses to a single number is precisely the\nfalse precision this layer exists to prevent, so it cannot be constructed. ``dist``\nrecords how the interior of the band is shaped for a consumer that samples it —\n``profiles`` means the band is the envelope of the discrete scenario corners (no\ndistribution is asserted between them), which is the honest default here.",
      "properties": {
        "low": {
          "title": "Low",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "central": {
          "title": "Central",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "high": {
          "title": "High",
          "type": "number"
        },
        "unit": {
          "title": "Unit",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "dist": {
          "default": "profiles",
          "enum": [
            "triangular",
            "uniform",
            "profiles"
          ],
          "title": "Dist",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "low",
        "central",
        "high",
        "unit"
      ],
      "title": "ScenarioBand",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "ScenarioConstant": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
